-- title:
--   Conjugation by a q-Hecke idèle preserves the level-ℓ Hecke set
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $\Lambda,R$ be $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ that are orders in the sense of the project's predicate [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11), i.e. each contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and is finitely generated; assume $R\le\Lambda$. Let $q,\ell$ be non-zero natural numbers with $\ell$ coprime to $q$. Let $n$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ lying in [`QuaternionAlgebra.primeHeckeSet R q`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_ClassSetHecke.html#L109), that is: $n$ lies in the finite-adèle box $\widehat{R}$ (the additive group generated by the $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in R$ and $\alpha$ everywhere integral), $q\cdot n^{-1}\in\widehat{R}$, while $n^{-1}\notin\widehat{R}$ and $q^{-1}\cdot n\notin\widehat{R}$. Let $\beta$ be a unit of the same ring whose component at $v$, under [`Submodule.finiteAdeleEvalAt`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L36), equals $1$ for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ not containing $\ell$. Then $n^{-1}\beta n$ lies in [`CerednikDrinfeld.levelHeckeUSet Λ R ℓ`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_ClassSetGraph.html#L44) if and only if $\beta$ does; membership in that set means lying in [`QuaternionAlgebra.primeHeckeSet R ℓ`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_ClassSetHecke.html#L109) together with $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\cap h\widehat{R}h^{-1}\neq R$ and $R\not\subseteq \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\cap h\widehat{\Lambda}h^{-1}$.
--
--   This is the invariance, under conjugation by an idèle of elementary divisors $(1,q)$, of the level-$\ell$ Hecke condition on idèles concentrated above $\ell$, for $\ell$ coprime to $q$; it is the local-global bookkeeping that makes the $\ell$-Hecke correspondence compatible with the $q$-structure on the class set. It is used in the computation of the pushforward of the class-set Hecke matrix attached to [`CerednikDrinfeld.levelHeckeUSet`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_ClassSetGraph.html#L44) along the intersection of orders.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_conj_mem_levelHeckeUSet_iff_of_mem_primeHeckeSet.lean

